{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>All the congregation.</b> The complete congregation — for the dead of the desert had already died, and these were set apart for life." "<b>And Miriam died there.</b> Why is the section of Miriam's death juxtaposed to the section of the red heifer? To tell you: just as offerings atone, so the death of the righteous atones (Mo'ed Katan 28)." "<b>And Miriam died there.</b> She too died by a kiss. And why was 'by the mouth of YHWH' not said of her? Because it is not a dignified way to speak of a woman. But of Aharon 'by the mouth of YHWH' is stated — in ״אֵלֶּה מַסְעֵי״ (Numbers 33)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:11:41.409230252Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}